<title>NORWAY: Norway C. Bank downgrades 1997 CPI to 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Norway C. Bank downgrades 1997 CPI to 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's central bank, Norges Bank, presented the following second-quarter forecasts for key economic indicators. The bank's first-quarter forecasts for 1997 made in March are included for comparison.</p>
<p>					    1997		     1998</p>
<p>							   March</p>
<p> Private consumption		  3.5	  (4.0)     3.25</p>
<p> Public consumption		   2.75	 (2.5)     1.75</p>
<p> Total gross investment	    10.25	 (8.5)     4.5</p>
<p> Mainland demand			4.0	  (4.0)     3.25</p>
<p> Export				   5.0	  (7.0)     6.5</p>
<p> Import				   7.0	  (8.25)    4.75</p>
<p> Overall GDP			    3.75	 (4.25)    4.0</p>
<p> Mainland GDP			   3.25	 (3.25)    3.0</p>
<p> Jobless rate			   4.0	  (4.5)     3.75</p>
<p> CPI					2.5	  (2.75)    2.0</p>
<p> Oil price per barrel (crowns)    130	  (129)     125</p>
<p> C/A pct surplus of GDP	     8.0	  (7.0)     8.0</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
